  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5590",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the interaction with CAKI-1 through a multi-step pathway involving the P2X purinoceptor 1, TE-9, and LB2241-RCC. These targets are all targeted by the same compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which suggests a common mechanism of action. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator of the P2X purinoceptor pathway, potentially influencing the activity of the downstream targets. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the shared interaction with the same compound suggests a possible role in the regulation of cellular processes mediated by these receptors. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Mollicellin N could interact with CAKI-1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
